    "description": "🎨 Affordable Art Rare Binder Builds — Part 2\n\n❄️ To celebrate the holidays and winter, today’s binder theme is a snow day! Not only does this span two binder pages, but we also use the “michi method!” For those who aren’t familiar with the term, it refers to using print outs to give your binders a more unique layout.\n\n💫 Art rares are a huge part of what got me back into collecting at the end of the Sword & Shield era and the start of the Scarlet & Violet era. With this series, I’m looking to spread the joy of collecting Japanese art rares with binder inspo.\n\n🙌🏼 You can copy my binder card for card, or take creative liberty and substitute out different cards you think would look better! For those looking for the English counterparts of today’s additions, you can find them below in order.\n\nVanillite 111/086 — White Flare\nVanillish 112/086 — White Flare\nMetagross 178/162 — Temporal Forces\nSnover 140/132 — Mega Evolution\nAbomasnow TG01/TG30 — Astral Radiance Trainer Gallery\nRaboot 147/142 — Stellar Crown\nSnorunt 188/182 — Paradox Rift\nWeavile ex 201/208 — Space-Time Smackdown (TCGP)\nSnom 168/162 — Temporal Forces\nMamoswine 160/208 — Space-Time Smackdown (TCGP)\nSwinub 165/159 — Journey Together\nReuniclus 212 — Scarlet & Violet Promos\nMagmortar GG03/GG70 — Crown Zenith Galarian Gallery\n\n✅ Follow @miraicardshop and check the link in bio for affordable Japanese Art Rares on our eBay!\n\n🤔 Should I replace any cards or do a specific theme next? Comment down below!",
